    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d254">

                <pb facs="0380" n="281" sameAs="frus:frus1936v05/pg281"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">832.5151/782: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Ambassador in Brazil</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Gibson</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1936-01-03T18:00:00-05:00">January 3, 1936—6
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>2. Your 346, December 21, 1 p.m.<anchor n="32" xml:id="d254-f1"/> Please inquire
                    of the Minister of Foreign Affairs<anchor n="33" xml:id="d254-f2"/> and, in your
                    discretion, of the Minister of Finance,<anchor n="34" xml:id="d254-f3"/> whether
                    the Brazilian Government has completed arrangements for funds to make a cash
                    payment to the American owners of frozen credits equivalent to that promised the
                    British creditors. Please cable.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
